  "result": "I added the `--json` flag to `quote`, plus a test file. All 8 tests pass (`python3 -m unittest discover`; pytest isn't installed). I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **`shop/cli.py`:** `quote` now takes `--json`. With the flag it prints `{\"total_cents\": N}`, using the same total it already calculated. Without the flag it still prints `fmt(total)` exactly as before.\n- **`tests/test_cli.py`** (new; the repo had no CLI tests):\n  - `test_json_output` checks that `quote a:10.00:1 --json` gives `{\"total_cents\": 1083}`.\n  - `test_default_output` checks that the plain output is still `10.83`.\n\nThe expected total is 1083 rather than 1000 because `calc_total` adds something on top of the 10.00 subtotal. The test checks what the code currently does, so if 10.83 is wrong, that's a problem in `calc_total` and not in this change.\n\nWhile checking the tests, a `git stash`/`pop` hit a conflict on `__pycache__` files and the stash was dropped. I checked the diff afterwards and only the intended changes are there. Running the tests also left untracked `__pycache__/` folders in `shop/`, `shop/carriers/` and `tests/`, which you can delete or add to `.gitignore`.",
